@spec picker_tiers_spec  src=tests/specs/picker_tiers_spec.lua  loc=209  cases=8
@harness   mk

# Intent
  Chrome-level pin for the by-copy catalogue picker: `tierPicker` lists both tiers in full, so a
  name held twice appears twice and neither copy hides the other, and `drawPicker` puts a create row
  at the head of each declared group, so a typed name lands in the tier you point at rather than a
  default nothing states. Recipe from picker_groups_spec, extended with picker_create_spec's Enter.

# Helpers
  @fn mkChrome(h)  @ 54-57
  @fn withCatalogue(harness, project, library)  @ 60-63
      -- A catalogue with `wobble` in both tiers -- the case a resolved list could not show.
  @fn labels(items, tier)  @ 65-69
  @fn frame(chrome, items, text, opts)  @ 73-84
  @fn rowsDrawn(drawn)  @ 86-90

# Cases
  @case 'both tiers are listed in full, so a name held twice appears in each'  [harness]  @ 96-106
  @case 'a name held in both tiers draws two rows alike, each under its own id scope'  [harness]  @ 110-122
  @case 'each row names the tier and the group it was drawn from, and wears no prefix'  [harness]  @ 126-138
  @case 'a non-exact filter offers to create in either tier, the project one first'  [harness]  @ 144-153
  @case 'Enter on a typed name creates in the project tier, the cursor resting there'  [harness]  @ 157-166
  @case 'an exact filter suppresses only its own group\'s create row'  [harness]  @ 170-183
  @case 'a declared tier with nothing in it still shows, so it can be created into'  [harness]  @ 187-195
  @case 'the groups survive a filter, there being two create rows to tell apart'  [harness]  @ 199-207

